      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Genus-level entry (hybrids). Watering is a mapping: Iowa State evenly moist, water thoroughly then let it dry a little; RHS never fully dry, never standing in water. The interval is RHS 'roughly once a week while growing', mapped by the agent, so from_knowledge_verify, not a measured value; it assumes a bark mix. Temperature: Iowa State days 70 to 80 F and nights 60 to 70 F, RHS keep above 16 C. Size: RHS 15 to 20 cm up to 50 cm tall, no spread, so unknown. Toxicity has one source (the ASPCA genus page); Iowa State and RHS pages say nothing on toxicity. Habit rosette is a mapping from RHS 'leaves in a clump'."
      },
